          "id": "f3b979cfff9292f16688b6271e1ae03091f28ae4",
          "message": "feat(sparq-kb): literature-ingestion scaffolding on FIXTURES, no live calls (sq-2489d.5) [OPUS-4.8] (#1187)\n\n* feat(sparq-kb): literature-ingestion scaffolding on FIXTURES, no live calls (sq-2489d.5) [OPUS-4.8]\n\nGenAI-KB Phase 5 (epic sq-2489d, design research/provenance-driven-genai-kb.md\n§4/§5). Adds the opt-in `literature` feature: the\n[connector]->[normalise]->[extract (record/replay)]->[ground]->[emit TTL]->\n[SHACL gate]->[sidecar] pipeline, exercised end-to-end over COMMITTED FIXTURES,\nmaking ZERO network and ZERO live-model calls. The live pilot is the separate,\ncredential-gated Phase-6 bead (sq-2489d.6, needs-access).\n\nWhat this ships (all behind the default-OFF `literature` feature; sparq-core/\nengine stay lean — `literature` pulls only serde_json, NOT the SPARQL engine):\n\n- crates/sparq-kb/src/literature/:\n  - connector: one OpenAlex-shaped adapter -> DOI-keyed, content-addressed SourceStubs.\n  - extract: the record/replay `Extractor` trait + `RecordedExtractor` (replays a\n    committed tape; the ONLY LLM-in-the-loop step, isolated so CI is offline).\n  - ground: the deterministic propose-then-verify grounding-resolver — a committed\n    Finding's justification must be an entailed span of the source abstract AND\n    every cited DOI must resolve to an in-batch pkg:Source; failures are\n    QUARANTINED to the sidecar, never silently dropped.\n  - pipeline: wires it all, emits machine-tier PROV-O Findings (wasDerivedFrom /\n    wasGeneratedBy / wasAttributedTo a pkg:MachineAgent, capped at secx:Conjectured\n    with a bounded confidence), and reports the Sidecar (citation-grounding rate +\n    quarantine list). The metric is COMPUTED at run time — no hard-coded number.\n- shapes/literature.shapes.ttl: the literature-tier SHACL guardrails (machine tier\n  != secx:Proven, confidence ceiling, no dangling cito:citesAsEvidence).\n- ontology/pkg/pkg.ttl + vocab.rs: net-new pkg:MachineAgent (prov:SoftwareAgent);\n  byte-pinned in vocab.rs (the bidirectional pin test stays green).\n- fixtures/literature/: a FABRICATED (illustrative, not captured) OpenAlex batch +\n  the frozen extraction tape; both carry deliberately-bad candidates (fabricated\n  span, dangling citation, Proven over-claim) so the quarantine + SHACL gate are real.\n\nGates (BOTH states green): cargo build/clippy --all-targets -D warnings/test in\ndefault (feature OFF) AND --features literature (and --all-features = close,literature);\nthe literature_pipeline integration test (#![cfg(all(literature, validate))]) runs the\npipeline over fixtures THEN runs the SHACL gate over the EMITTED TTL — the real path,\nproving the emitted graph conforms AND the literature shapes FIRE on an injected\nviolator AND a hand-authored Proven Finding is unconstrained. rustdoc --all-features\n-D warnings clean; readme-template 0 deviations (README 120 lines); privacy-claims +\nno-perf-numbers clean; new fmt applied to net-new files only. Wired a\nfeature-matrix.yml leg (`literature,validate`) so the net-new cfg-gated test EXECUTES\n(the #1171 silent-skip lesson).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs(sparq-kb): fix default-feature rustdoc broken intra-doc links in literature.rs [OPUS-4.8]\n\nThe always-compiled module-level //! docs referenced items that live in\n#[cfg(feature = \"literature\")]-gated submodules (extract::Extractor,\nextract::RecordedExtractor, pipeline::Sidecar, pipeline::MACHINE_AGENT_IRI,\nground). Under DEFAULT features those modules are not in scope, so\n`RUSTDOCFLAGS=\"-D warnings\" cargo doc --workspace --no-deps` failed with\nrustdoc::broken-intra-doc-links — the real failure behind the gating\n`clippy (gate) + fmt` lane (the bundled rustdoc-deny-warnings step, exit 101).\n\nFix per the #1202/#1212/#1222 established pattern: demote the six cross-references\nin the crate-level docs to plain `code spans`, noting they are `literature`-feature\nitems. The one remaining [`extract::RecordedExtractor`] intra-doc link is on a\n#[cfg(feature = \"literature\")] const, so it only compiles when the feature is on and\nresolves there.\n\nVerified clean in BOTH feature states with -D warnings:\n- cargo doc -p sparq-kb --no-deps (default) and --all-features\n- cargo doc --workspace --no-deps (the exact gate command, default features)\n- cargo clippy -p sparq-kb --all-targets --all-features -- -D warnings\n- cargo test -p sparq-kb (default) and --all-features (all suites pass)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Jesse Wright <jmwright.045@gmail.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>",
